TYPES.md §6.3, §7.5, EVALUATION.md §8.1, log-2026-11-01 "EVAL-OWED review FAIL": a check reading self's
identity runs once per identity of an instance: lr has none and equals j2's entry, j1's entry does not, so
both checks, bare self and self through a method, fail at j1[y] alone.
-- project.canon --
project acme {
  canon: "0.1"
}
-- a/a.canon --
/// A.
package a

/// A row.
record Row {
  /// Its code.
  code: String
  /// Its value.
  v: Int

  /// Whether self is j2's entry.
  fn isJ2(self) -> Bool { return self == j2["y"] }

  check inJ2: self == j2["y"] else "self is not j2's entry"

  check viaFn: isJ2() else "isJ2 is false"
}

/// A row.
let lr: Row = { code: "y", v: 2 }

/// Keyed by code, holding lr.
let j1: [Row] keyed by code = [lr]

/// Keyed by code, holding lr.
let j2: [Row] keyed by code = [lr]
-- build.txt --
error[E5001]  a/a.canon:20:15
  j1[y]: isJ2 is false
  expected by a/a.canon:16 (check viaFn)

error[E5001]  a/a.canon:20:15
  j1[y]: self is not j2's entry
  expected by a/a.canon:14 (check inJ2)

2 errors, 0 warnings in 1 package (…)
